\title{brownstone: Brownstone Plots: Manhattan Plots that Also Show Effect Sizes}
\description{
Draws Brownstone plots, a successor to the GWAS Manhattan plot. Alongside the usual -log10(P) skyline it shows each locus's effect size and its uncertainty on an aligned track beneath the chromosome axis, encodes minor allele frequency so that rare and common variant signals can be read on the same figure, and labels lead variants with their nearest gene (or any label you supply). Built on 'ggplot2' with a clean, modern theme.
